; wrapped false, exposing two flat top-level modules (Obs_eio, Obs_trace),
; is a deliberate choice, re-examined and reaffirmed after audit feedback —
; not an unexamined default. The collision risk that got the main module
; renamed from the bare, generic `Obs` to `Obs_eio` doesn't carry over to
; `Obs_trace` with the same force: a short generic word like `Obs` is likely
; to already exist, independently, in many observability-adjacent
; codebases, but a two-word compound like `Obs_trace` is not. The directly
; relevant local precedent is kafka-eio-core (../kafka-eio/kafka-eio-core/
; lib/dune in this same author's already-published sibling package): one
; wrapped-false library exposing four flat modules (Kafka_raw, Kafka_error,
; Kafka_consumer_handle, Kafka_security) together, not nested — the same
; shape as here, already through this same audit process. Full wrapping
; (nesting Obs_trace under Obs_eio) remains available later without being
; a breaking change for most callers if this judgment call is revisited.
(library
 (name obs_eio)
 (public_name obs-eio)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules obs_trace obs_eio)
 (libraries eio mtime))
